From 3cfa9cab40402e3461af4c22b94d527f478e4cb0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ClozyA <133191303+ClozyA@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 09:35:03 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] MAS local: keep window size and position across lean
 rotations

Repeatedly toggling the lean title bar's rotate button shrank the
window by 1-2 px each turn and let its position drift when one
orientation had to be pushed onto the screen (ModAVD#249):

- EmulatorQtWindow::doResize() scaled through QSize::scaled(...,
  Qt::KeepAspectRatio), which truncates to integers, and then took
  min(widthScale, heightScale). Combined with skin_window_resize()'s
  ceil(layout * scale), a 1080p window at 1098x618 lost 1-2 px on
  every doResize round-trip (1098x650 -> 617x1129 -> ... -> 1093x647).
  Compute the floating-point scale directly in lean_window::scaleToFit()
  with an IEEE-754 ceil guard, and skip redundant doResize() calls in
  EmulatorContainer when guestAreaSize() already matches the guest
  widget size.
- Remember the pre-rotation frame and guest size in
  lean_window::RotationMemory across lean turns so turning back
  restores both the previous size (even if the other orientation was
  shrunk by fitInto() to fit the screen) and the previous position
  (even if the other orientation was clamped to a screen edge). Moving
  the window between turns forgets the saved position; resizing,
  maximizing or snapping clears the saved state.

Refs ModAVD/ModAVD#249
